  "description": "This Planning Statement supports a planning application for the retention of an external terrace, boundary treatment, decking and retractable canopies at The Robin public house, 397A High Road, Wembley. The application is submitted in response to enforcement case reference E/25/0148.\nThe development has been in place for approximately 14 years and serves a critical function in ensuring public safety by providing a controlled, designated outdoor area for customers. Without this provision, customers would be required to remain on the public pavement with drinks, creating hazardous conditions for pedestrians and an unmanageable situation for the business.\nThe premises operates under a valid Street Trading Licence (No. 10725), for which an annual fee of £1,300 is paid to Brent Council. ",
